messages:
maya: Heads-up — I'm running a short workshop tomorrow to align on Console per-route KPIs with kernel-aware attribution. Goal: show p50/p95/p99, throughput, error rate, plus token-level waterfall and KV hit/miss. Want to avoid exploding cardinality.

sam: SGTM. What's the proposed sampling strategy? We can't afford full-tagging for every request.

kevin: Proposal: sample 1% of requests per route and attach lightweight tags: kernel_name, batch_size_bucket, kv_hit boolean, seq_len_bucket. That should keep cardinality controlled and still give actionable signal.

bindu: UI note: per-route header should surface p50/p95/p99 inline, then a compact token waterfall below collapsed by default. Click to expand -> per-kernel split (sparklines for each kernel). Also add a smallcard for throughput and errors.

maya: Also thinking of instrumenting kernel-selection cause so we can attribute regressions: fields kernel_reason = {default, fall_back_capacity, manual_override}. If p99 jumps we need to know whether it's due to kernel fallback.

metrics-bot: ingest-projection: sampling 1% with the extra kernel tags projects ~+8% metric throughput and ~+6% storage. Approve to proceed? :chart_with_upwards_trend:

ryan: We should also capture kv_miss_reason: warmup|eviction|cold_start. Right now misses are ambiguous. Showing miss_reason breakdown alongside kv_hit-rate will help triage perf regressions that look like cache misses but are actually warmups.

maya: Draft proto for telemetry (simplified):
```
message RoutePerfPoint {
  string route_id = 1;
  string kernel_name = 2; // e.g. 'kv-optimized-v2'
  string kernel_reason = 3;
  bool kv_hit = 4;
  string kv_miss_reason = 5; // warmup|eviction|cold_start
  int32 batch_size_bucket = 6;
  int32 seq_len_bucket = 7;
  int64 token_latency_p50 = 8;
  int64 token_latency_p95 = 9;
  int64 token_latency_p99 = 10;
  int64 total_tokens = 11;
  int32 error_count = 12;
}
```

sam: LGTM. Minor tweak: rename seq_len_bucket -> seq_bucket to keep proto short. Also we should record kv_ttl_bucket maybe later.

bindu: For Console UX, let's add these views: 1) route header (p50/p95/p99, qps, err rate); 2) token waterfall (collapsed) with hover showing per-kernel token break; 3) filter pill for kernel, seq_bucket, kv_hit; 4) alert threshold config (p99 > baseline * 2). Can we add a compact per-kernel timeline sparkline in the route list?

maya: Agree. Ops checklist: runtime needs to emit kernel_name and kernel_reason at kernel selection point, runtime should emit kv_miss_reason when miss occurs, and telemetry pipeline needs sampling + enrichment to compute per-route reservoir samples by (kernel, seq_bucket). I'll draft a one-pager and a minimal dashboard prototype tomorrow.

kevin: FYI: when we add kernel tag we should also forward kernel version hash (short) in the sampled events so we can diff regressions between kernel builds.

metrics-bot: action: marked approved for prototype sampling. Estimated cost delta flagged for review with finance.

maya: Thanks all — workshop invite sent. If anyone has example dashboards or queries you'd like included, drop them here before EOD. :calendar:
